  "problem": "Suppose $a=[1,\\,-5]^{T}$ and $b=[5,\\,1]^{T}.$ Find the Manhattan distance between $a$ and $b.$\n\n${d}_{1}(a,b)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the Manhattan distance is defined as\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}(a,b)=‖a-b{‖}_{1}\n$$\n\nwhere for an $N$-dimensional vector $v,$\n\n$$\n‖v{‖}_{1}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{N}|{v}_{i}|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{1}(a,b) & =‖a-b{‖}_{1} \\\\  & ={‖[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]‖}_{1} \\\\  & =|1-5|+|-5-1| \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
